{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.PhaseBlockResolution","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhaseBlockResolution","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Units.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fin.VecNotation","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhaseBlockResolution.floor_bar_even_units","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhaseBlockResolution.floor_bar_even_units","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhaseBlockResolution.lean#L125-L130","doc":"The bar-evenness in the form the narrative uses, with `q` a unit and its\nbar-image the honest inverse. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhaseBlockResolution.floor_bar_defect","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhaseBlockResolution.floor_bar_defect","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhaseBlockResolution.lean#L117-L123","doc":"The cross-multiplied identity is genuinely conditional on `u · v = 1`: off\nthat locus the two sides differ by `3(u²−v²)((uv)²−1)`. Recorded so the theorem\nabove is not mistaken for a `ring` tautology. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhaseBlockResolution.floor_bar_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhaseBlockResolution.floor_bar_even","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhaseBlockResolution.lean#L93-L115","doc":"**The commutator floor is bar-even.**\n\nStated division-free by cross-multiplication, and with the bar involution\n`q ↦ q⁻¹` carried by the single hypothesis `u · v = 1`, so the statement needs\nnothing beyond `CommRing`:\n\n`floorNum v · floorDen u = floorNum u · floorDen v`.\n\nThe identity is not a tautology of the shape — over a general commutative ring\n`floorNum v · floorDen u − floorNum u · floorDen v = 3(u²−v²)((uv)²−1)`, which\nis nonzero in general and vanishes exactly on the bar-involution locus `uv = 1`.\n\nWhy it matters on `qou-cds1`. The sibling prune `MarkovWeightsConventionD` shows\nboth surviving convention-D Markov weights are bar-even, hence that no bar-odd\npart can be assembled *from the weights*. The floor is not built from weights —\nit is a non-trace functional evaluated on the very component every weight\nannihilates — so that prune does not reach it. This says the trace-invisible\nsector supplies no bar-odd material either, and the prune therefore extends\nrather than breaking. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhaseBlockResolution.floorDen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhaseBlockResolution.floorDen","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhaseBlockResolution.lean#L90-L91","doc":"Denominator of the commutator floor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhaseBlockResolution.floorNum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhaseBlockResolution.floorNum","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhaseBlockResolution.lean#L81-L88","doc":"Numerator of the commutator floor `net(d_C) = −(q²−1)² / (q⁴+q²+1)`, the\n`z`-free part of the ladder phase: the value of the coordinate sum on the\ncomponent of `Δ` lying in `[H,H]`, which every trace annihilates.\n\nWritten as a function of a bare ring element so that the bar involution can be\napplied to it without leaving `CommRing`; `q` and its bar-image `q⁻¹` are then\nrelated only by the hypothesis `q · q⁻¹ = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhaseBlockResolution.chi_two_one_delta_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhaseBlockResolution.chi_two_one_delta_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhaseBlockResolution.lean#L55-L77","doc":"**The 2-dimensional block character annihilates `Δ`.**\n\nThe `λ = (2,1)` block of `H₃(q)` is two-dimensional and each generator `σᵢ` acts\nthere with eigenvalues `q` and `−q⁻¹`, hence with trace `h = q − q⁻¹`. Those two\nfacts alone force `χ^{(2,1)}(Δ) = 0`:\n\n`(h²/2)·2 − (h/2)·h − (h/2)·h = h² − h²/2 − h²/2 = 0`.\n\nNote what the statement does *not* need: the character's values on the three\nlonger basis elements are left completely free, because `Δ` has zero coordinate\nthere. So the vanishing is a property of `Δ`'s support together with the block's\ndimension and generator trace — not of the block's full character table.\n\nConsequence for the ladder: the eigenphase `α = (ε − tr_M)/2` is blind to the\n2-dimensional block **in every convention**, since no Markov parameter enters\nthis identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhaseBlockResolution.pair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhaseBlockResolution.pair","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhaseBlockResolution.lean#L50-L53","doc":"A linear functional on `H₃(q)` applied to a coordinate vector: the pairing\nof its values on the six basis elements against the vector. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhaseBlockResolution.deltaCoords","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhaseBlockResolution.deltaCoords","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhaseBlockResolution.lean#L44-L48","doc":"Coordinates of `Δ = NF(n) − NF(p)` in the Gröbner–Shirshov basis\n`[γ, σ₀, σ₁, L₊, L₋, e⁻]` of `H₃(q)`, with the Hecke parameter `h = q − q⁻¹`.\nThis is the vector the Q_β ansatz evaluates. ","signatureChunk":0}]}